  "term": "prion disease",
  "definition": "Prion disease is a group of degenerative disorders of the nervous system in humans and animals linked to abnormal prions. They may arise through genetic, infectious, or sporadic causes and in humans commonly involve dementia, problems with coordination, and a fatal course.",
